00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.530
So with that said,
let's get into it.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.720
First, Mike, thank you
so much for being here.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:24.250
Would you mind
starting by telling

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.830
us a little bit about Niantic
architecture and scale

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:28.280
and your role there?

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:29.530
MICHAEL DEBRECENI: Absolutely.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:33.160
So I am a site reliability
engineer with Niantic.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:35.220
I'm actually the
first dedicated SRE

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:38.380
and have been with the
company for about three years.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.780
When Pokemon Go launched,
I wasn't with Niantic yet,

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:42.947
but I was definitely
an avid player.

00:01:42.947 --> 00:01:44.530
I was fascinated by
some of the growth

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:48.410
and scaling challenges at launch
